Usage: sort [-bcdfghinMruVz] [-s] [-m] [-o FILE] [-R|--sort=random] [--random-source=FILE] [-k KEY] [-t CHAR] [-c|-C] [-S SIZE] [-T DIR] [--batch-size=N] [FILE...]
{{help:help:0}}
{{help:version:0}}

Large inputs use temporary disk runs and require filesystem write access.
-S/--buffer-size selects an accounted byte budget (default units: KiB).
-T/--temporary-directory may repeat; --batch-size uses at most 16 merge inputs.
{{help:numeric-sort:0}}
Nonzero percentage buffer sizes require an unavailable physical-memory query.
Option values and operands after -- remain literal during alias normalization.
